The assessment is finished. The last open item turned out not to be a bug.

The one open probe: Claude Code 2.1.309 fixed transcripts that broke when long tool output was cut in the middle of an emoji. I checked whether my code has the same problem by searching for every place it cuts strings at a byte position. The four places that needed a closer look are all safe:
• repl.rs:516 only removes a trailing \, which is one byte.
• commands_spawn.rs and prompt.rs check that the cut falls between characters before cutting.
• tools.rs:544 cuts at a length worked out just before the cut.

My audit log stores only usage numbers, not tool output, so that bug has nothing to cut there. This was a reading of the code, not a run with emoji output. The assessment now marks it "probed, nothing found, not a task candidate".

Where the file is: session_plan/assessment.md, 58 lines. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the file isn't committed but is on disk for the planner, and the working tree is otherwise clean.

